From d8e5afd3b531abb6cb6d3ec6817295cdb86402ca Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: phlink <phlink@local>
Date: Wed, 29 Apr 2026 18:06:40 +0530
Subject: [PATCH] phlink: phase 08-01b color mixer foundation
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Lay the type-safe foundation for the phlink appearance subsystem:

* Add 11 kColorPhlink* role token IDs (CONTEXT D-01, D-08):
  Canvas, Surface, SurfaceAlt, Card, Text, TextMuted, Hairline,
  Accent, OnAccent, Danger, Success.
* Wire PHLINK_COLOR_IDS into the CHROME_COLOR_IDS umbrella in
  chrome/browser/ui/color/chrome_color_id.h so phlink IDs participate
  in the chrome color id map (no re-seed of kChromeColorsStart).
* Add chrome/browser/ui/color/phlink_color_mixer.{cc,h} exporting
  AddPhlinkColorMixer(provider, key); register it in
  AddChromeColorMixers AFTER AddNativeChromeColorMixer and BEFORE
  the key.custom_theme block (CONTEXT D-02): brand identity wins
  over native vibrancy, but a user-installed community theme still
  wins over phlink.
* Add chrome/browser/ui/color/phlink_palette.{cc,h} declaring
  kPhlinkLight[] and kPhlinkDark[] palette arrays (zero-filled
  placeholders; patch 0111 fills Light, patch 0112 fills Dark).
* Add chrome/browser/ui/color/phlink_color_mixer_unittests.cc
  (CONTEXT D-12) — parametrised over ColorMode::{kLight,kDark},
  asserts every kColorPhlink* resolves to non-placeholder color
  and that double-registration is idempotent.
* Wire new sources into chrome/browser/ui/color/BUILD.gn and
  the unittest into chrome/test/BUILD.gn unit_tests target.

Patch slot 0110 per CONTEXT D-09. No telemetry; no IPC surface;
site isolation untouched.
